 and methods used to produce high-assay low-enriched uranium (HALEU) and Lithium-6 for the advanced nuclear fuels target end market. Its Specialist Isotopes and Related Services segment engages in the research and development of technologies and methods used to separate high-value, low-volume isotopes, such as C-14, Mo-100 and Si-28, for target end markets, including pharmaceuticals and agrochemicals, nuclear medical imaging, and semiconductors; provision of related services; and operation of PET labs. The company offers the Aerodynamic Separation Process (ASP) technology, which separates gas species and isotopes in a volatile state; and the Quantum Enrichment (QE) technology, which separates isotopes. It also produces and commercializes Molybdenum-100, Molybdenum-98, and Ytterbium-176 for the nuclear medical industry. In addition, the company develops Zinc-68, Nickel-64, and Xenon-129/136 for the nuclear medical industry; Lithium-7, Uranium-235, and Chlorine-37 for the energy industry; and Germanium-70/72/74 for semiconductor markets. The company was incorporated in 2021 and is based in Dallas, Texas.","employees":271,"website":"https://aspisotopes.com","country":"United States","city":"Dallas","officers":[{"name":"Ms. Heather  Kiessling","title":"Chief Financial Officer"},{"name":"Mr. Robert  Ainscow","title":"Chief Operating Officer"},{"name":"Mr. Nicholas Michael Mitchell","title":"Co-Chief Operating Officer"}]},"sector_medians":{"fpe":7.016,"tpe":7.885,"ps":1.531,"pfcf":10.79,"peg":0.84,"pb":1.389,"ev_ebitda":4.651,"rev_growth":0.241,"eps_growth":0.907,"eps_growth_fwd":0.2295,"eps_growth_next":0.1078,"div_yield":0.025,"roe":0.1011,"roa":0.05131,"de":19.53,"gross_margin":0.3585,"op_margin":0.1609,"profit_margin":0.07225,"current_ratio":1.885},"valuation":[{"k":"fpe","label":"Forward P/E","v":null,"sector":7.016,"verdict":"—"},{"k":"tpe","label":"TTM P/E","v":-1,"sector":7.885,"verdict":"Loss-making"},{"k":"ps","label":"Price / Sales","v":9.975,"sector":1.531,"ve